WEBVTT

00:12:58.246 --> 00:13:03.454
Luckily, all great theater provides
the opportunity for transformation.

00:13:04.329 --> 00:13:09.079
We can use this intermission
to stop, breathe, observe,

00:13:09.079 --> 00:13:13.162
and use our imaginations to create
a more beautiful world onstage and off,

00:13:13.162 --> 00:13:14.871
one that is more equitable,

00:13:14.912 --> 00:13:16.079
more reflective

00:13:16.079 --> 00:13:17.537
and more just.

00:13:18.704 --> 00:13:22.829
As Prior says at the end of Tony Kushner’s
masterpiece about the AIDS epidemic,

00:13:22.871 --> 00:13:24.162
"Angels in America,"

00:13:25.287 --> 00:13:26.579
"I'm almost done.

00:13:26.579 --> 00:13:28.662
The fountain's not flowing now,

00:13:28.662 --> 00:13:31.287
they turn it off in the winter,
ice in the pipes.